&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who/What is Artefact?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Artefact is a next-generation strategy and data consulting firm dedicated to transforming&amp;nbsp;organizations through data and AI. We combine the rigor of top-tier strategy consulting&amp;nbsp;with deep expertise in data, digital, and analytics to help clients achieve tangible&lt;br&gt;business impact.&lt;br&gt;With 1,800+ consultants, data scientists, and engineers across 23 countries, we work&amp;nbsp;with global leaders such as Samsung, L’Oréal, Orange, and Sanofi. Our Zurich office is&amp;nbsp;at the heart of Artefact’s growth, advising clients on their most pressing strategic&amp;nbsp;challenges — from AI strategy and governance to digital transformation roadmaps and&amp;nbsp;new business model design.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Main Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;As a AI Manager in Pharma &amp;amp; Life Science in our Zurich office, you will be at the intersection of strategy consulting and data/AI innovation. You will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategy Development: &lt;/strong&gt;Work with client leadership teams (specifically in the Pharma &amp;amp; Life Sciences sector) to address high-stakes questions: How can AI reshape our business model? How should we govern and organize for data? Which strategic programs deliver the most impact?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Structured Problem-Solving:&lt;/strong&gt; Break down complex challenges into clear,&amp;nbsp;actionable recommendations, using frameworks and methodologies rooted in&amp;nbsp;classic strategy consulting, enriched by Artefact’s data and AI expertise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Project Delivery:&lt;/strong&gt; Support engagements end-to-end, from hypothesis framing&amp;nbsp;and market/competitor analysis to client workshops, governance design, and&amp;nbsp;implementation roadmaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Client Engagement:&lt;/strong&gt; Collaborate closely with C-level stakeholders and business&amp;nbsp;unit leaders. You’ll build trusted relationships, communicate recommendations&amp;nbsp;with clarity, and ensure strategic alignment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Knowledge &amp;amp; Practice Building:&lt;/strong&gt; Contribute to the growth of Artefact’s Zurich&amp;nbsp;office by shaping new offerings, creating intellectual capital (frameworks, thought&amp;nbsp;pieces, benchmarks), and participating in business development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Management: &lt;/strong&gt;Lead, mentor, and foster collaboration within hybrid project teams, ensuring high-quality delivery and team growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Candidate Profile&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an ambitious, analytically minded talent who is passionate about&amp;nbsp;leveraging data and AI to solve business problems. The ideal candidate meets several&amp;nbsp;of the following qualifications:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education:&lt;/strong&gt; Bachelor’s and Master’s degree (preferred) in Business,&amp;nbsp;Engineering, Computer Science, Economics or a related field. An excellent&amp;nbsp;academic track record is highly valued.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; Approximately 5–8 years of experience in strategy consulting with a mandatory focus on the Pharma &amp;amp; Life Sciences sector and&amp;nbsp;with a proven track record of delivering data, analytics, or AI-driven transformation projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;10,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Pharma Domain Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong grasp of the life sciences ecosystem, including regulatory environments, the drug development lifecycle, and digital health trends.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Business Acumen &amp;amp; AI Fluency:&lt;/strong&gt; A strong dual affinity for business and technology. You possess a deep understanding of modern data and AI concepts (e.g., Generative AI, LLMs, predictive machine learning, cloud architectures) and their practical business applications. While you do not need to be a programmer, you must be capable of scoping AI use cases and confidently discussing tech constraints and opportunities with c-level stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong knowledge of data and digital technologies&lt;/strong&gt; (e.g. analytics, AI, machine learning concepts, digital marketing, cloud platforms) is expected – you should be tech-savvy and eager to deepen your understanding of the data/AI domain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analytical &amp;amp; Problem-Solving Skills:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong quantitative and analytical skills,&amp;nbsp;with an ability to draw insights from data. You have an analytical mindset and are&amp;nbsp;comfortable handling data-driven analysis to support decision making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication &amp;amp; Interpersonal Skills:&lt;/strong&gt; Excellent communication skills, both&amp;nbsp;written and verbal. You can present complex ideas clearly and can adapt your&amp;nbsp;message to both technical and non-technical audiences. Experience creating&amp;nbsp;impactful presentations or reports is a must. You also enjoy working&amp;nbsp;collaboratively in teams and liaising with clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Languages:&lt;/strong&gt; Fluency in German and English (both written and spoken) is&amp;nbsp;mandatory; French is a strong plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Eligibility:&lt;/strong&gt; You must be eligible to work in Switzerland.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategy with a Data Edge:&lt;/strong&gt; Artefact is not a traditional strategy consultancy nor&amp;nbsp;a pure tech player — we sit uniquely at the crossroads, giving you the chance to&amp;nbsp;build boardroom-level strategy expertise while being at the forefront of AI and&amp;nbsp;digital transformation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Zurich Office Impact:&lt;/strong&gt; As part of a growing Swiss team, you will have visibility&amp;nbsp;and impact from day one. You will help shape Artefact’s footprint in the region&amp;nbsp;and work directly with senior leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learning &amp;amp; Growth:&lt;/strong&gt; Regular training in both strategy consulting methodologies&amp;nbsp;and AI/data capabilities, combined with international exposure.• Culture of Doers: Innovation, Action, Collaboration. We are entrepreneurial,&amp;nbsp;fast-moving, and committed to delivering impact — while supporting each other’s&amp;nbsp;growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is based in &lt;strong&gt;Zürich&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Don’t worry if you don’t meet all the criteria! We value motivation, pragmatic problem-solving, and potential above all else. We’d love to hear from you and learn more about your passion for driving the AI revolution.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

